    {
      "title": "Stateless Services",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 1,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Stateless Services",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. What Stateless Means",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==Stateless==: any instance can serve any request",
                "No per-user state in {red:instance memory} or {red:local disk}",
                "Sessions → ==Redis==, files → ==S3==, data → database",
                "Or carry state in a signed token (==JWT==)"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Stateless vs Stateful",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                "Stateless",
                "Stateful"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Instances",
                  "interchangeable",
                  "unique"
                ],
                [
                  "Kill, replace, autoscale",
                  "{green:freely}",
                  "{red:risky}"
                ],
                [
                  "Needs",
                  "nothing extra",
                  "sticky routing or replication"
                ]
              ],
              "highlightRow": 1
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Example: Session in Redis",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "Request 1",
                    "sub": "Server A saves session",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Redis",
                    "sub": "key = session ID cookie",
                    "ink": "red"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Request 2",
                    "sub": "Server B reads it, still logged in",
                    "ink": "green"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "4. Mistakes",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "In-memory session behind an LB → random logouts",
                "Local-disk uploads → missing files"
              ],
              "style": "cross",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Fix",
              "text": "Use a ==shared store==. Sticky sessions are a crutch, not the fix."
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "**Interview Point: why not keep sessions in memory?** The next request may hit an instance without them.",
                "**Stateless vs sticky sessions?** Sticky pins a user to one server; stateless needs no pinning."
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Load Balancers: L4 vs L7",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 2,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Load Balancers: L4 vs L7",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. What a Load Balancer Is",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "One ==entry point==: a VIP or DNS name",
                "Spreads traffic across **healthy** backends",
                "Hides backend addresses"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. L4 vs L7",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                "L4 (transport)",
                "L7 (application)"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Reads",
                  "IP + TCP/UDP port",
                  "HTTP host, path, headers, cookies"
                ],
                [
                  "Wins",
                  "speed, any protocol",
                  "path/host routing, TLS termination, rewrites, sticky cookies"
                ],
                [
                  "Cost",
                  "no content awareness",
                  "more CPU per request"
                ],
                [
                  "Example",
                  "AWS NLB",
                  "AWS ALB, Nginx, HAProxy"
                ]
              ],
              "highlightRow": 1
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "Client",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "LB",
                    "sub": "VIP / DNS name",
                    "ink": "purple"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Backends",
                    "sub": "healthy only",
                    "ink": "green"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Mistake",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "The LB is a SPOF",
              "text": "Run it redundantly: ==multi-AZ==, active-passive, or DNS/anycast across several LBs."
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "4. Interview Point",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "**Path routing needs which layer?** L7, it reads the HTTP path",
                "**Why pick L4?** Speed, low overhead, any TCP/UDP protocol",
                "**How avoid an LB SPOF?** Several LBs: multi-AZ or DNS/anycast"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Balancing Algorithms and Health Checks",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 3,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Balancing Algorithms and Health Checks",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Picking a Server",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Algorithm",
                "Picks",
                "Best when"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "==Round robin==",
                  "Next server in order",
                  "Equal servers, similar request cost"
                ],
                [
                  "==Weighted RR==",
                  "Bigger servers get more requests",
                  "Mixed server sizes"
                ],
                [
                  "==Least connections==",
                  "Fewest active connections",
                  "Uneven or long-lived requests"
                ],
                [
                  "==IP hash==",
                  "Same client or key, same server",
                  "Affinity, cache locality"
                ]
              ],
              "highlightRow": 2
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "{green:Consistent hashing} limits remapping when servers join or leave",
                "Plain hash by server count remaps **most** keys on a change"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Health Checks",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "LB probes each backend every ==N seconds==",
                "Probe: TCP connect, or HTTP `GET /health` expecting ==200=="
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "Probe",
                    "sub": "every N s",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Failure threshold",
                    "sub": "reached",
                    "ink": "red"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Removed",
                    "sub": "no traffic",
                    "ink": "orange"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Success threshold",
                    "sub": "reached",
                    "ink": "green"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Re-added",
                    "sub": "serves again",
                    "ink": "green"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Common Mistakes",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "**Shallow** `/health` returns 200 while the DB is down",
                "**Deep** check hits the DB: one DB blip removes every instance at once",
                "No ==connection draining== on removal drops in-flight requests"
              ],
              "style": "cross",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Health check depth",
              "text": "Check the instance itself and its must-have dependencies, but never let one shared dependency fail ==all== instances together. Always **drain** before removal."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Latency, Throughput and Estimation",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 4,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Latency, Throughput and Estimation",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Latency vs Throughput",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                "Latency",
                "Throughput"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Measures",
                  "Time for one request",
                  "Requests or bytes per second"
                ],
                [
                  "Unit",
                  "ms: report ==p50/p95/p99==",
                  "QPS / RPS, bytes/s"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==concurrency = throughput x latency== (Little's law)",
                "200 RPS x 50 ms = {blue:10 requests in flight}",
                "More instances raise throughput, not per-request latency",
                "p99 climbs near 100% load: keep utilization ==60-70%== (30-40% headroom)"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Estimation Recipe",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "Average QPS",
                    "sub": "DAU x actions/day / 86,400",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Peak",
                    "sub": "2-3x average",
                    "ink": "orange"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Storage",
                    "sub": "writes/day x size x retention",
                    "ink": "purple"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Bandwidth",
                    "sub": "QPS x payload size",
                    "ink": "green"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Example",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "10M DAU x 10 requests / 86,400 = ==1,150 QPS== average",
                "Peak is about ==3,000 QPS==",
                "3,000 / 500 per instance = 6 instances",
                "Add one spare: ==7== for N+1"
              ],
              "style": "number"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "4. Common Mistakes",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Sizing for average load, not **peak**",
                "Ignoring p99 and watching only the average",
                "Forgetting 1 day is about ==100,000 s== (quick rounding)"
              ],
              "style": "cross",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "red"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
